---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<Prose
  title="Terms of use"
  description={`The terms that apply when you use ${SITE.name}, including the safety disclaimer for our repair guides.`}
  lede="Please read the safety section. It is the part that actually matters."
  updated="8 August 2026"
>
  <p>
    By using <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong> you agree to these terms. If you don't
    agree, please don't use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>1. General information only</h2>
  <p>
    Everything on {SITE.name} is general information for a general audience. It
    is not professional advice and it is not tailored to your home, your
    plumbing, your wiring, your device or your body. Buildings, fixtures and
    devices vary enormously by country, age and manufacturer. An animation shows
    the typical case; yours may differ.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Safety — please read</h2>
  <p>
    You are responsible for deciding whether a job is within your ability, and
    for doing it safely. In particular:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Stop if you smell gas.</strong> Leave the building and call your
      gas emergency number. Do not troubleshoot it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Do not work on mains electrical circuits</strong> unless you are
      qualified and it is legal for you to do so where you live.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Turn off the water supply</strong> before opening any plumbing,
      and know where your main shut-off is before you start.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Never mix drain chemicals</strong>, and never use a plunger or an
      auger on a drain you have already poured chemicals into.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Seek medical help</strong> for any injury, or for symptoms like
      numbness, discolouration or loss of movement. Our guides are not medical
      advice.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If a guide's warnings describe your situation, stop and call a qualified
    professional. To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.name} accepts no
    liability for loss, damage or injury arising from following, or failing to
    follow, anything published here.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Your use of the site</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>scrape the site at a rate that degrades it for other people;</li>
    <li>
      republish our animations or written guides as your own, in whole or in
      substantial part;
    </li>
    <li>
      use the site for anything unlawful, or attempt to interfere with its
      operation or security.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The text, illustrations, animations, code and design on this site are
    © {new Date().getFullYear()} {SITE.name} unless stated otherwise. You may
    link to any page, quote a short passage with attribution, and print pages
    for your own personal use. Anything beyond that needs written permission —
    ask at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Brand names and product names mentioned in guides belong to their owners and
    are used descriptively. Mentioning a product is not an endorsement by, or an
    affiliation with, its manufacturer.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    This site displays third-party advertising. Ads are labelled and kept
    visually separate from our content. We do not control which specific ads are
    shown and an ad appearing here is not an endorsement. See our
    <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for how advertising cookies work.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided "as is". We don't promise it will always be available
    or error-free, and we may change, move or remove any page at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The date at the top of this page shows the
    current version, and continuing to use the site after a change means you
    accept it.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a
    >.
  </p>
</Prose>
